# Klein

Klein is a dev tool for Go web apps using [templ](https://templ.guide). It compiles `.templ` views into Go under `.klein/`, builds the app, and runs a dev server with hot reload.

## Project layout

Dashboard Klein app lives under `backend/dashboard/`:

- `backend/dashboard/views/` — source `.templ` files (edit these)
- `backend/dashboard/.klein/views/` — generated Go (do not edit)
- `backend/dashboard/.klein/hotreload/` — generated hot-reload code (do not edit)
- `backend/dashboard/public/` — static assets
- `backend/dashboard/klein.config` — paths config (`views`, `klein`, `public`)
- `tailwind.conf` — optional Tailwind config

## Commands

| Command | When to use |
|---------|-------------|
| `klein init [--here]` | Scaffold a new project |
| `klein dev` | Start dev server + file watcher (blocks, uses port 5490 by default) |
| `klein check` | **Verify changes without starting a server** |
| `klein check --tailwind --test` | Full validation: build + CSS + tests |
| `klein tailwind init` | Add Tailwind to an existing project |

## Agent workflow

**Use `klein check` to verify work — not `klein dev`.**

`klein dev` starts a long-running server on port 5490 and will conflict if one is already running. After editing views or Go code, run:

```bash
klein check
```

Exit 0 = compiles; exit 1 = fix the reported templ/build/test error.

Only suggest `klein dev` when the user explicitly wants to run the app locally.

## Editing rules

- Edit `backend/dashboard/views/**/*.templ`, never `backend/dashboard/.klein/views/**/*.go`
- In templ files, import hot reload as `<module>/dashboard/.klein/hotreload`
- Run `go build` directly only if Klein is unavailable; prefer `klein check` in Klein projects
